{#
  prevention.j2
  Generates specific, evidence-based prevention tips for a diseased crop.
  Called by treatment_path after treatments are generated.
  Uses RAG-retrieved knowledge base content for accuracy.
#}

Generate specific disease prevention tips for a {{ plant_identified }} farmer
who has just been diagnosed with {{ diagnosis.name if diagnosis else "a crop disease" }}.

Disease Category: {{ disease_category | default("unknown") }}
Severity: {{ diagnosis.severity if diagnosis else "unknown" }}

{% if retrieved_context %}
━━ KNOWLEDGE BASE — USE THIS INFORMATION IN YOUR PREVENTION TIPS ━━
The following content is from authoritative agricultural documents.
You MUST base your prevention tips on this verified information.
Do NOT give generic advice — use the specific details below:

{% for chunk in retrieved_context %}
[Source: {{ chunk.document_name }}]
{{ chunk.chunk_text }}

{% endfor %}
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
{% endif %}

REQUIREMENTS FOR PREVENTION TIPS:
✓ Give 5-7 specific, actionable prevention tips
✓ Each tip must be directly relevant to {{ diagnosis.name if diagnosis else "this disease" }} on {{ plant_identified }}
✓ Reference specific practices that prevent THIS disease — not generic farming advice
✓ Include timing (e.g. "before rainy season", "every 14 days", "at planting")
✓ Mention Uganda/East Africa context where relevant (agrovets, local extension officers, NARO)
✓ Include at least one tip about resistant varieties if available
✓ Include at least one tip about crop rotation or field hygiene
✓ Include at least one tip about monitoring and early detection

{% if disease_category == "fungal" %}
FUNGAL PREVENTION FOCUS:
- Emphasise reducing humidity and leaf wetness
- Mention preventive fungicide rotation to avoid resistance
- Include drainage and spacing recommendations
- Mention removing crop debris after harvest
{% elif disease_category == "bacterial" %}
BACTERIAL PREVENTION FOCUS:
- Emphasise tool disinfection between plants
- Avoid overhead irrigation
- Remove infected material immediately
- Use certified disease-free seed or planting material
{% elif disease_category == "viral" %}
VIRAL PREVENTION FOCUS:
- Control insect vectors (aphids, whitefly, thrips)
- Use certified virus-free planting material
- Rogue out infected plants immediately
- Mention resistant varieties available in Uganda
{% elif disease_category == "insect" %}
PEST PREVENTION FOCUS:
- Regular scouting frequency and timing
- Biological control options available locally
- Crop rotation to break pest cycles
- Use of pheromone traps where available
{% endif %}

{% if personality == "friendly" %}
Write in simple, encouraging language a smallholder farmer can understand.
Mention local resources (agrovets, extension officers, NARO Uganda).
{% elif personality == "formal" %}
Use precise agronomic language with specific timings and rates where known.
{% elif personality == "concise" %}
Give exactly 5 tips, one sentence each. Be direct and specific.
{% endif %}

Respond ONLY with a valid JSON array of strings.
Each string is one complete prevention tip.
No markdown, no backticks, no extra text.

Example:
[
  "Apply a copper-based fungicide preventively every 14 days during the rainy season — available at most Ugandan agrovets",
  "Plant certified disease-resistant tomato varieties such as Tengeru 97 or Cal J recommended by NARO Uganda",
  "Remove and burn all crop debris after harvest — never compost infected material as spores survive"
]